# Deliberately NO SPA catch-all.
#
# Every real route is prerendered to a static file at build time, so Netlify
# serves them directly. A `/* /index.html 200` rule would make every bad URL
# return the homepage with a 200, which Google indexes as a duplicate and
# reports as a soft 404. Without it, unmatched paths fall through to 404.html
# and return a real 404.
